      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Kaylee@,\n\nCould you please review this patch?\n\nThis patch addresses a DCHECK failure in PartitionAlloc caused by a mismatch in strict aliasing rules between Skia (enabled explicitly) and Chrome (disable explicitly). The patch disables strict aliasing for PartitionAlloc by adding `-fno-strict-aliasing` to its build config flags, aligning its original configuration.\nWhat are your thoughts on this?\n\nInterestingly, it seems that most Google codebases, compile everything with `-fno-strict-aliasing`. Are you aware about any specific reason Skia does use `-fstrict-aliasing`? Should we consider doing the same for Skia Standalone?\n\nOne reason might be keeping Skia compatible with the widest possible set of embedders. I might want to add a comment explaining the reason in the code, if you want.\n\nThanks,",
      "revId": "547d5e894fa8e9871c4c74374a61cfc5cbae0b26",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
