      "writtenOn": "2024-11-20T16:50:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At the very least, this is incorrect. \"Strict aliasing\" (or just glvalue access rules C++20 7.2.1.11, note that the rules in C++ are somewhat different than C, such as not making `unsigned char` special) is just how C and C++ work, breaking these rules produces undefined behavior. The use of `-fno-strict-aliasing` is to instead use a non-standard dialect of C or C++ (and one which isn\u0027t super well defined). Compiler optimizations are a completely separate issue.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 755,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 755,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "547d5e894fa8e9871c4c74374a61cfc5cbae0b26",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
